# Core architecture

## Data flow

Browser (`components/`) → `fetch /api/*` → Route Handlers (`app/api/`) → `lib/*` → Supabase (auth/profiles) + HydraDB / OpenAI.

## Server-only secrets

API keys and external clients live only in `lib/*` (and Route Handlers that call `lib/*`). Never read `process.env` for secrets in client components. `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` is server-only (seed scripts).

## Authentication

- **Supabase Auth**: OAuth (Google, GitHub, Azure) + email/password
- **Postgres** (`profiles`, `access_events`, `admin_actions`) with **RLS**
- **Middleware** ([`middleware.ts`](middleware.ts)): session refresh, route gating by `account_status`
- **API guards** ([`lib/auth.ts`](lib/auth.ts)): `guardApprovedApi()` on memory/ask/brain routes; `guardAdminApi()` on admin routes
- New users: `pending_approval` until admin approves; 3 failed auth attempts → `blocked` (admin unlock)
- HydraDB: per-user `sub_tenant_id` = `user_<auth.users.id>`

## MVP constraints (do not add unless explicitly requested)

- No background jobs, Redis
- No global state libraries (Redux, Zustand, React Query)
- File uploads limited to audio/Markdown in existing API routes

## Next.js 16

This project uses Next.js 16 with breaking API changes. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using App Router features. Heed deprecation notices.

## Where code belongs

| Concern | Location |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP validation + response | `app/api/*/route.ts` |
| Auth session + guards | `lib/auth.ts`, `lib/supabase/*` |
| Business logic, SDK calls | `lib/*.ts` |
| Zod schemas | `lib/validation.ts` |
| Shared types | `lib/types.ts` |
| UI | `components/` (feature) or `components/ui/` (shadcn primitives) |
| DB migrations | `supabase/migrations/` |
